status: accepted_deviation
exit: 0
note: |
  Form C. `main` nested INSIDE `place Entry { }`. It is a deviation: `place Entry`
  is a marker, `main` belongs at the top level, as in every examples/ project. Mains
  moved inside `place Entry` make the book diverge from the corpus with no compiler
  signal.

  The compiler accepts it (it compiles and runs, exit 0), and the gate asserts
  exactly that, so the ledger says what the compiler does. A checker that rejects a
  nested main makes this fixture fail compilation; `status` then becomes
  reject_clean, with the `match` fragment of the new error.
